docker run -d --name <c-name>  -p <host port no:c-port no>  <i-name>

docker run :- it will do three things 1. it will pull the image from docker hub if not present in the server, 2. it will create the container, 3. it will start the container.

-d:- detached mode :- you are going to running the container in a background

--name: container meaningful name and name should be unique - login

-p:- port mapping

Host port:- it will be decide by the DevOps Team and it will be unique port number. 

Container or app port number:- it will be decide by the dev team, same port number you can use for no.of containers.

i-name: provide a docker image name


container life cycle 
===============

docker create :- it will only create the container 
docker run :- it will do three things 1. it will pull the image from docker hub if not present in the server, 2. it will create the container, 3. it will start the container.
Docker ps:- to see only running contianers
docker ps -a:- to see all containers including stopped containers aslo
docker stop:- it will stop the contianer
docker restart:- to restart container
docker pause:- to pause the container
docker rm:- to delete only stopped containers
docker rm -f :- to delete running container by force remove
docker inspect:- To see container details

